.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "mystrfunctions.h"

int mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcpy()
function copies the string pointed to by
.I src
(including the terminating null byte) into the buffer pointed to by
.I dest .
The caller must ensure that
.I dest
is large enough to hold the copied string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, returns the number of characters copied (not including the
null byte). Returns \-1 if either
.I dest
or
.I src
is NULL.
